      "side": 1,
      "message": "tInterframeGap governs the maximum possible USB-PD packets over PD. (Plus some additional math for minimum packet length itself.) Empirical measurements show 6.240ms for 3 packets + interframe gap. \n\nI believe this frequency should be set to be greater than the maximum possible valid physical traffic pattern. Otherwise anything that chats at \u003e40msg per second -- say, firmware update over PD, specific AltModes, or battery temperature reading -- will be broken.\n\nPD3.0 Extended Descriptors are another problem. Or Apple Charger serial number readout. Those get very chatty very quickly.\n\n(1 second / 6.240ms * 3 messages \u003d~ 481 messages/second max valid.)",
